{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CjRKxb2jbUmZ6yDxvipsaF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# WI-282 — train build commits: enforce the `WI:` trailer at commit time\n2\t\n3\t**WI:** WI-282 · **Status:** queued · **Delivers:** the train commit contract\n4\t(harness floor; no spine SR — meta harness layer, empty-`SR-Refs` precedent)\n5\t\n6\t## Problem\n7\t\n8\tLive failure, 2026-07-23, train `p0-g3-WI-281-9ae9`: session 006's build\n9\tcommit `45637d2` was written with a malformed trailer block — `Train:`/`Base:`\n10\tpresent, **no parseable `WI: WI-281` trailer** (an interposed blank line breaks\n11\tgit's trailer block). `reviewed_train_head()` resolves a train's reviewed head\n12\tas *the newest commit carrying a `WI:` trailer*, so the integrator's verdict\n13\tgate skipped `45637d2`, resolved the head to the older `d8d50e6`, read its\n14\tCHANGES-REQUESTED (005) instead of the tip's APPROVE (007 at `45637d2`), and\n15\tparked the train `rework` — **a one-line commit-message slip cost a full extra\n16\tbuild+review cycle.** The trailer rule is currently prose (worker prompt);\n17\tenforcement-audit doctrine: a rule the harness can check must not be left to\n18\tprose.\n19\t\n20\t## Approach\n21\t\n22\t- **Primary — a commit-time floor check.** A `commit-msg` hook (the floor is\n23\t  currently pre-commit only; the message is only checkable in commit-msg),\n24\t  shipped in `project-trajectory/hooks/` with the same thin meta-repo wrapper\n25\t  pattern as `.githooks/pre-commit`: on a branch matching `llm/train/*`, a\n26\t  commit that touches non-generated files must carry a parseable\n27\t  `WI: WI-<n>` trailer — refuse with a message naming the exact fix.\n28\t  Scope carefully: the dispatcher's own sanctioned shapes (`Blocked-WI:`\n29\t  dispositions, `integrate:`/`telemetry:`/`review:` commits) must stay legal —\n30\t  gate on \"touches non-generated files\" and/or exempt the sanctioned subject\n31\t  prefixes.\n32\t- **Secondary — a loud integration diagnostic.** When `reviewed_train_head()`\n33\t  resolves to a commit that is NOT the newest substantive commit on the train\n34\t  (i.e., trailered head ≠ tip-most non-telemetry commit), journal a warning\n35\t  naming both SHAs — so a slipped trailer is visible at integration instead of\n36\t  masquerading as honest dissent.\n37\t- Tests beside the existing hook tests (worktree case included — hooks run in\n38\t  train worktrees via the shared `core.hooksPath`); downstream: hooks ship in\n39\t  the kit, so note the migration in the close deliverable.\n40\t\n41\t## Interfaces\n42\t\n43\tNo cross-module seam — intra-module (hooks + `agent_dispatch.reviewed_train_head`\n44\tdiagnostic + tests).\n45\t\n46\t## Done-when\n47\t\n48\t- [x] A train-branch build commit without a valid `WI:` trailer is refused at\n49\t      commit time with an actionable message; sanctioned dispatcher shapes\n50\t      unaffected (tests prove both). — a pure-sh floor in `hooks/commit-msg`\n51\t      (no new module, per the spec's intra-module design; holds without Python);\n52\t      `tests/test_commit_msg_wi_trailer.py`.\n53\t- [x] The reviewed-head mismatch diagnostic journals loudly (test). —\n54\t      `agent_dispatch.warn_reviewed_head_slip` journals `reviewed-head-trailer-slip`\n55\t      naming both SHAs; `tests/test_agent_loop_integrate.py`.\n56\t- [x] Commit bar green; row `done`, spec archived. — bar green; the `done`\n57\t      flip + spec archival is the integrator's close-ritual at done-flip (WI-287).\n58\t\n59\t**Downstream migration:** the floor is the existing shipped `hooks/commit-msg`\n60\t(bootstrap already maps `hooks/commit-msg` → `.githooks/commit-msg`), so an\n61\tadopted repo picks it up on the next `downstream-resync` with no new file to\n62\tregister; it is vacuous off `llm/train/*`, so a repo not running parallel\n63\tdispatch pays nothing.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e57370e-8fa5-48cc-ac58-efd3fa70d438","uuid":"4c7e16cd-1113-4de0-b177-10a2b8351cac","timestamp":"2026-07-24T09:22:16.208Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\p0-g3-WI-282-eb40\\docs\\specs\\WI-282.md","content":"# WI-282 — train build commits: enforce the `WI:` trailer at commit time\n\n**WI:** WI-282 · **Status:** queued · **Delivers:** the train commit contract\n(harness floor; no spine SR — meta harness layer, empty-`SR-Refs` precedent)\n\n## Problem\n\nLive failure, 2026-07-23, train `p0-g3-WI-281-9ae9`: session 006's build\ncommit `45637d2` was written with a malformed trailer block — `Train:`/`Base:`\npresent, **no parseable `WI: WI-281` trailer** (an interposed blank line breaks\ngit's trailer block). `reviewed_train_head()` resolves a train's reviewed head\nas *the newest commit carrying a `WI:` trailer*, so the integrator's verdict\ngate skipped `45637d2`, resolved the head to the older `d8d50e6`, read its\nCHANGES-REQUESTED (005) instead of the tip's APPROVE (007 at `45637d2`), and\nparked the train `rework` — **a one-line commit-message slip cost a full extra\nbuild+review cycle.** The trailer rule is currently prose (worker prompt);\nenforcement-audit doctrine: a rule the harness can check must not be left to\nprose.\n\n## Approach\n\n- **Primary — a commit-time floor check.** A `commit-msg` hook (the floor is\n  currently pre-commit only; the message is only checkable in commit-msg),\n  shipped in `project-trajectory/hooks/` with the same thin meta-repo wrapper\n  pattern as `.githooks/pre-commit`: on a branch matching `llm/train/*`, a\n  commit that touches non-generated files must carry a parseable\n  `WI: WI-<n>` trailer — refuse with a message naming the exact fix.\n  Scope carefully: the dispatcher's own sanctioned shapes (`Blocked-WI:`\n  dispositions, `integrate:`/`telemetry:`/`review:` commits) must stay legal —\n  gate on \"touches non-generated files\" and/or exempt the sanctioned subject\n  prefixes.\n- **Secondary — a loud integration diagnostic.** When `reviewed_train_head()`\n  resolves to a commit that is NOT the newest substantive commit on the train\n  (i.e., trailered head ≠ tip-most non-telemetry commit), journal a warning\n  naming both SHAs — so a slipped trailer is visible at integration instead of\n  masquerading as honest dissent.\n- Tests beside the existing hook tests (worktree case included — hooks run in\n  train worktrees via the shared `core.hooksPath`); downstream: hooks ship in\n  the kit, so note the migration in the close deliverable.\n\n## Interfaces\n\nNo cross-module seam — intra-module (hooks + `agent_dispatch.reviewed_train_head`\ndiagnostic + tests).\n\n## Done-when\n\n- [x] A train-branch build commit without a valid `WI:` trailer is refused at\n      commit time with an actionable message; sanctioned dispatcher shapes\n      unaffected (tests prove both). — a pure-sh floor in `hooks/commit-msg`\n      (no new module, per the spec's intra-module design; holds without Python);\n      `tests/test_commit_msg_wi_trailer.py`.\n- [x] The reviewed-head mismatch diagnostic journals loudly (test). —\n      `agent_dispatch.warn_reviewed_head_slip` journals `reviewed-head-trailer-slip`\n      naming both SHAs; `tests/test_agent_loop_integrate.py`.\n- [x] Commit bar green; row `done`, spec archived. — bar green; the `done`\n      flip + spec archival is the integrator's close-ritual at done-flip (WI-287).\n\n**Downstream migration:** the floor is the existing shipped `hooks/commit-msg`\n(bootstrap already maps `hooks/commit-msg` → `.githooks/commit-msg`), so an\nadopted repo picks it up on the next `downstream-resync` with no new file to\nregister; it is vacuous off `llm/train/*`, so a repo not running parallel\ndispatch pays nothing.\n","numLines":64,"startLine":1,"totalLines":64}}}
